# Writing a post

Posts live in `src/content/posts/<slug>.md` and publish to `/writing/<slug>/`.
Everything below renders at build time — never add a `<script>` to a post.

```yaml
---
title: "The title"
description: "One sentence, used for search results and the archive list."
date: 2026-09-21
draft: true   # flip to false to publish
---
```

Draft a new post with `draft: true` so the author can review it at
`/writing/<slug>/` before it appears in any list, then flip the flag.

## Syntax

**Maths** — `$\sigma(z)_i$` inline, `$$ … $$` on its own lines for display. KaTeX.

**Diagrams** — a fenced `dot` block becomes inline SVG via Graphviz.
Mermaid is *not* supported; convert any mermaid to DOT.

````markdown
```dot
digraph {
  rankdir=LR;
  node [shape=box style=rounded color="#c8cad0" penwidth=1.1];
  Proposer -> Verifier [label="candidates"];
}
```
````

Default `fontname`/`fontsize`/transparent background are injected unless the
source sets `fontname` itself. Keep palettes grey (`#c8cad0`, `#8b8e97`).

**Figures** — captions auto-number as `Fig. 1.`, `Fig. 2.` per article, so never
write the number by hand. Add `wide` to spill past the 672px reading column.

```markdown
:::figure{src="/images/ladder.svg" alt="Four bars of increasing length."}
Caption text, which may contain *emphasis*, `code` and [links](/writing/).
:::
```

To caption a diagram, nest it in the same directive:

````markdown
:::figure{wide}
```dot
digraph { a -> b }
```
The caption must be the LAST paragraph; everything above it is the figure body.
:::
````

**Callouts** — `:::note`, `:::aside`, `:::warning`, optional title in brackets:

```markdown
:::note[A small aside]
A useful detail that would break the flow of the argument.
:::
```

**References** — ordinary Markdown footnotes (`[^key]`) collect themselves into a
styled list at the end. Use these for citations rather than a hand-rolled list.

## Richer visuals

For anything DOT cannot express (annotated, multi-layer explanatory figures),
hand-author an SVG into `public/images/` and reference it with `:::figure{src=…}`.
Set a `viewBox`, no fixed `width`/`height`, `role="img"` and an `aria-label`; use
`Inter, system-ui, sans-serif` and the greys above so it matches the page.

A table of contents appears automatically at 3+ `##`/`###` headings — don't write one.

## Verify

Always finish with `npm run check`. Plain `npm run build` reuses a cached content
store, which hides a broken diagram behind an empty but successfully built page;
`check` clears that cache first and exits non-zero on a bad DOT block.

To look at the result, `npm run dev` and open the post (`npx astro dev stop` after).
